Once upon a time, in the lush jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, a Gnome Warlock named Zephyr was on a quest to gather rare herbs for his latest potion. His loyal Succubus, Zara, floated beside him, her ethereal beauty a stark contrast to the dense foliage. As they ventured deeper into the jungle, they encountered a group of hostile pirates. Zephyr quickly summoned his Succubus to fight, but to his surprise, Zara vanished into thin air. Confused, Zephyr realized that Zara had used her stealth ability, becoming invisible to the pirates. She then swiftly dispatched them, leaving Zephyr amazed at her cunning.

The answer to the riddle is that Succubi have the stealth ability, which makes them invisible to enemies. This ability is not commonly known, leading to the misconception that Voidwalkers are more popular than Succubi for leveling and questing. However, the stealth ability actually makes Succubi a better choice in many situations. [end of text]


